From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Nguyen <tungnh@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:24:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] Notify UrlListManager observers on destruction

PopupBlockerTabHelper and FramebustBlockTabHelper are owned by
tabs::TabFeatures, which is torn down during tab close before the
WebContents teardown that closes an open content setting bubble. The
"Pop-ups blocked" and "Redirect blocked" bubble models observe the
helpers' UrlListManager, so they can outlive the manager they observe.

Add UrlListManager::Observer::OnUrlListManagerDestroying(), called from
the manager's destructor, and have both bubble models stop observing in
response. Also make the bubble models' OnListItemClicked() handle the
tab helper no longer being available.

(cherry picked from commit b3e0c169981773e1e839561cf2ca2198ba244829)

